settings-system-permissions-platform-s-security-features-redactor-tool = The platform's security features — the Redactor, the Tool & Commands Guard, the Classifier — protect your machine on a best-effort basis: they judge what a guarded harness asks and redact what leaves. They are not a sandbox, and a wider grant is a wider reach for a harness the guard cannot stop; the refusals over ~/.ssh, keys and the like still apply.
settings-system-permissions-recommended-productivity-without-macos-fences-app = Recommended for productivity: without it, macOS fences the app off from Library, Documents on a managed Mac and other users' folders, and an agent or a probe working there fails on the fence rather than the work.
settings-system-permissions-these-grants-macos-s-read-asked = These grants are macOS's, read and asked for by the desktop app; a browser session can hold the switches but cannot ask. The switches still say what the platform may rely on.
