settings-system-permissions-turned-here-but-macos-has-granted = You turned it on here, but macOS has not granted it — nothing of ours can use it until you do that in System Settings.
settings-system-permissions-turning-asks-macos-once-app-s = Turning it on asks macOS once, with the app's own usage description; after a refusal, only System Settings can change the answer. Turning it off here revokes nothing — it only stops the platform from using the grant.
settings-system-permissions-turning-opens-system-settings-privacy-security = Turning this on opens System Settings › Privacy & Security › Full Disk Access; add Bisa there. The grant is per app — the bundled app, not a development binary.
settings-system-permissions-voice-mode-which-coming-nothing-listens = For voice mode, which is coming. Nothing listens today, and nothing of ours will open the microphone while this is off.

