settings-ssh-panel-arrow-hostname = → { $hostname }
settings-ssh-panel-no-git-host-blurb = Your <code>~/.ssh/config</code> names no git host. A profile binds a key without one; a Host block is the other way — an alias like <code>git-github-work:owner/repo</code> that reaches one host with one key — and you paste it yourself.
settings-ssh-panel-offline-blurb = Offline — <code>ssh -G</code>, nothing reaches the host.
settings-ssh-panel-read-by-node-blurb = SSH is read by the node from your own SSH directory. A node started without SSH answers 503 here; the CLI's <code>bisa git ssh keys</code> reads the same.
settings-people-panel-invite-expiry-blurb = Expires in { $expires } (<code>collab.invite_ttl_hours</code>). Whether a valid code admits at once or waits on you is <code>collab.join</code>, in the Workspace settings.
